@startuml workspace-restore
title US-15: Workspace Restore - Returning Operator Resumes Scoped Stream

skinparam sequenceArrowThickness 1.5
skinparam participantBorderColor #555555
skinparam participantBackgroundColor #F8F8F8
skinparam noteBorderColor #AAAAAA
skinparam noteBackgroundColor #FFFDE7

actor Operator
participant "Angular\nDashboard" as Dashboard
participant "Google\nOAuth" as Google
participant "Express API" as API
database "TimescaleDB\nusers + user_workspaces" as TSDB

== Authentication ==

Operator -> Dashboard : opens Sentinel dashboard\n(returning user)

Dashboard -> Google : initiate OAuth flow\n(silent if Google session active)

note over Google
  If the operator's Google session is still valid,
  Google issues a new ID token without a popup.
  The operator sees no interruption.
end note

Google --> Dashboard : Google ID token

Dashboard -> API : POST /auth/google\n{ id_token: <Google ID token> }

API -> Google : verify ID token\n(google-auth-library)
Google --> API : { sub: "google_user_id", email: "..." }

API -> TSDB : INSERT INTO users (google_sub, email, last_login_at)\nON CONFLICT (google_sub) DO UPDATE\nSET last_login_at = now()\nRETURNING user_id

TSDB --> API : { user_id: "uuid-..." }

API --> Dashboard : { jwt: "<signed token>", expires_in: 28800 }

note over Dashboard
  JWT is stored in memory only - not localStorage,
  not a cookie. It lives for the browser session.
  On tab close, the operator re-authenticates on
  next open (Google silent auth makes this seamless).
end note

== Workspace Load ==

Dashboard -> API : GET /users/me/workspace\nAuthorization: Bearer <JWT>

API -> TSDB : SELECT scope FROM user_workspaces\nWHERE user_id = $1

TSDB --> API : { geo_region: { name: "France", bounds: {...} },\n  entity_types: ["aircraft","vessel"],\n  alert_types: ["SIGNAL_LOSS","COMPOSITE"] }

API --> Dashboard : saved scope

Dashboard --> Operator : map restores to France region\nalert type filters pre-selected\nno scope prompt shown

== Stream Resume ==

Dashboard -> API : WebSocket upgrade\nGET /stream?token=<JWT>

API -> TSDB : SELECT scope FROM user_workspaces WHERE user_id = $1
TSDB --> API : scope

note over API
  Scope is loaded into the in-memory connection map.
  Only alerts matching this scope will be pushed.
  The operator receives alerts from the moment the
  connection opens - no replay of missed alerts.
  Historical investigation uses US-14 instead.
end note

API --> Dashboard : 101 Switching Protocols

Dashboard --> Operator : alert stream active\nexact same view as previous session

@enduml
